1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:05:37,640
Part 8 stopped on an unfinished sentence. On coming to Vrindavan, one should come having planned. For the elder residents, for the monkeys, for the pigeon, for the peacocks, this much gram is to be given, or fruit is to be given. All of this should be kept in the estimate from before. This much is to be distributed. But when he takes the articles, then it is noticed that these monkeys have been here two by two from before. The children would play with the monkeys in this way. The monkeys would threaten, would make a face, and the children would do the same. Many would threaten, we will study the Veda, and these would do the same. Many children stayed busy in this. Making faces. A change, making a mouth, speaking. And leaping on the branches. They would keep swinging on the branches like the monkeys. A monkey is swinging, so they also are swinging. They are going from one branch to another. In Vrindavan the trees did not stay very high. Some did, but some stayed close to the ground. On those they would swing, they would walk. And the frog. Bheka is the name of the frog. They would leap with the frogs. They throw the whole body in a leap, so the children also, seeing them, some go leaping like that. As many times as the frog leaped, that many times these also leaped. Those leaped on the feet, sitting. And leaping like this, with the frog, here and there. And sometimes they would jump into the water of the rivers. They wanted to cross the small rivers by a jump. There was a contest, who will cross the river. Small hill rivers. Sometimes they would bathe, and then the ornamenting would start. They would jump with the frogs, sometimes make a dam. And they would see their own shadow in the water, and laugh. They themselves would laugh, and the shadow would also laugh. And seeing that, these would laugh. And they would say, come, come. They would do it in that way. And there was an echo. It would strike the hill. They would speak loudly, and a voice would come from there also. They would keep speaking in this way. And they would curse the echo. When the echo came, they would abuse the echo. Who is it. From there the speaking was, who is it. On this, they would scold. We are coming, we are coming, we will tell you. In this way they would scold their own speech. It always went on like this. These are some of the names of the sports that were given. The children who would curse their own echo, the meaning of cursing is not that they abused the way children of now abuse. With heroism, and they would speak very high talk. I am such a hero. Then from there he would say, I am such a hero. Then they would say, what are you in front of me. Quiet. Speaking in this way. They did not abuse. Children of a very well taught community, they kept provoking their own echo. By this a teaching is found. The children are teaching this, as it were. From their conduct it should be learned that a person in the world becomes unhappy by himself. He accepts in the mind, this is my praise, or this is my insult. So the children, agitated by their own speech, are scolding it, why are you speaking like this.

2
00:05:38,890 --> 00:11:22,700
Saying this happiness of the children, the play with Krishna, Shukadeva Goswami says, in this way, he who is experienced as the joy of Brahman by the saints, as the supreme deity by those who have attained service, and as a human child by those under illusion, with him the heaps of accumulated piety played. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.12.11] This verse was very dear to Srila Prabhupada. Again and again, in his writings, he quoted it. Those children who in very many births had done a great deal of piety, had done good acts, had done the devotion of the Lord, they played in this way with Sri Krishna. Ittham means in this way. Meaning, in this way, in many ways, they were sporting with Krishna. Together they played. They were sporting with the Lord. They experience him as the joy of Brahman. They accept that the joy of Brahman is a good source, and they experience the joy. They are able to experience it only in meditation. But with Brahman they never receive a chance to play, to give the embrace of the neck. Like the sages beginning with Sanaka. They meditate on the Lord, and a chance to play with the Lord has never come to them. Great persons whom illusion can never bind. Who are above attachment to all the things made by illusion. In a thing produced by illusion they have not even a little attachment, and in Brahman, in the form of the Lord, whose mind has become stopped, they are called sat. Many times in the Bhagavatam. And asat is said of one who is absorbed in enjoying the things of the world, in taking pleasure. So satam means those who in their life have chosen the Lord. They have understood the Lord alone. And in front of the Lord, worldly things cannot give them any happiness. Even the happiness of heaven tastes flat to them. Enjoyment, liberation, nothing feels good. They stay overwhelmed in the form of the Lord. So they are called sat. Then the great saintly persons, the liberated persons, speak about Lord Krishna. They say this, that Sri Krishna is the Supreme Brahman, and by thinking of the Supreme Brahman they receive happiness. They accept, Krishna is the Supreme Brahman, Brahman condensed as eternity, knowledge, and bliss. But they are able to experience that happiness of the Lord only in meditation. They only contemplate. And by those who have attained service, as their supreme deity. Higher even than these saints are they who have attained service. Who have accepted Sri Krishna as their worshipful Lord, and who worship in the feeling of a servant. They serve the Lord. Who have a contact with the Lord, with his limbs. And in the eternal world, in Vaikuntha, or even in this world, who serve the Lord. Service. The meaning of dasya is service. And taking oneself as low, taking the Lord as supremely great, the Lord of all, the master of all, the Lord, they serve. They serve with great love. So such devotees are called those who have attained service. They have attained the position of a servant. But what do they take Krishna to be. The supreme deity. They take him as their own supreme god. They take him as the worshipful Lord. They serve in every way. But even those associates who live in Vaikuntha do not receive a chance to play with the Lord in this way. And the one whom the devotees of the servant's feeling take as the supreme deity, take as the worshipful Lord, take as the Lord, with that same Lord these children are playing.

3
00:11:24,930 --> 00:17:28,300
As a human child, by those who have taken shelter of illusion. And there is one class. Maya has two meanings. One is the illusion of his own form, and the other is the great illusion. First we take the meaning of the energy of his own form. Those who have taken shelter of maya. People who are under the energy of the Lord's own form, like Nanda Maharaj and the rest, or any resident of Braj. Then in their eye, what is Krishna. A human child. A boy of a human being. The children are playing with him. And the second meaning is, people who are under the great illusion. Whose intelligence illusion has taken away. There is no knowledge. In their eye, what is Krishna. A human child. A boy of a human being. So each his own eye. Who understands Krishna as what. As the joy of Brahman, as the supreme deity, as a human child. All three are being said of Krishna alone. The same Lord who is playing with the children appears to the saints as the experience of the joy of Brahman. And to the devotees of the servant's feeling, as the worshipful Lord. On this, Shukadeva Goswami's hint is that if any person develops the feeling in himself like these children, then finding the Lord in the form of his own friend, he can sport with him. He is in truth within the range of the senses, and he is within the range of speech. And that same Lord, having come within the range of every sense, is playing in Braj. So the point is said three times. It should not be understood that the Lord who plays with the children is someone else, and the realization of Brahman that the great saints make is someone else. No. This same child. Of him people have the experience in the form of Brahman. Of him they have the experience in the form of the worshipful Lord. And of him foolish people have the experience in the form of an ordinary human child. Some people do not want to see the Lord with the eye. Some people are such, they know everything. They stay sunk in meditation. And the Lord can be seen with the eye also. An embrace can be given. Talk can be had with him. But in their mind meditation is the chief thing. In their mind the wish itself does not come, let us talk with the Lord. Some fortunate ones are such that they see the Lord in the mind. The rest, who make a show of meditation, mostly sleep. Nowadays we have seen it many times. The eyes were closed. They know that meditation should be done with the eyes closed. Its meaning is that another sight should not be seen. This is right. Let him keep the body straight, with the eyes closed. But with the eyes closed, something is to be seen. Not seeing alone will not become meditation. Not seeing is a separate process. But the meaning of seeing is, the yogis see him with the mind fixed in meditation and gone to him. Inside, they see the Lord. The yogis do the lila. But how long will they be satisfied by meditating. The gopis say to Uddhava. The residents of Vrindavan say, by holding meditation, how long will we give ourselves patience. With whom we have danced, whose ornament we have done. They meditate on this same Krishna as the experience of the joy of Brahman. The meaning is, the obstruction of all the things of the material ground is done. After that the joy begins which is called the joy of Brahman. Then the joy of Brahman has many kinds. Higher than that is the happiness in which there is a personal relation with the Lord. Service. Those who have attained service. But the highest is playing with the Lord.

4
00:17:30,720 --> 00:20:51,640
The Lord says in the Chaitanya-charitamrita, the friend, the pure friend, climbs on my shoulder. Who are you, a great person. My friend, the pure friend, climbs on my shoulder. And when I do not let him climb on the shoulder, he says, who are you, a great person. You and I are equal. What great person have you become, that you will not let me climb on the shoulder. The Lord had lost in the game. And the game was going, that whoever wins will become the rider, and whoever loses will become the horse. This game was going. Then Hari lost, Sridama won. Surdas sang it, this Hari lost, and Sridama won. Then Sridama said, you become the horse. Then Krishna said, I will not become it. Why. I am Nanda Maharaj's boy. I am a king's boy. Then, in a game, what is a king and a pauper. In playing, who is the master. In playing, all are equal. Then Sridama says, when it was time to climb, at that time you climbed. And you say, I am a king's son. If you will not become the horse, we will not keep you in our game. Come, will you become it or not. All said, come, move, move. They removed Krishna from that field by force. The one put out. Come, move. We will not keep him. We will not play. And that same Lord, condensed bliss, now with his face hanging, quiet. And the children say, come, play. These people begin to play. The children are all playing, calling. Someone sometimes is speaking some word. By then Sri Krishna begins to weep. The Lord also begins to weep without his devotees. After that Sridama says, now, when you become the horse. They are weeping. Krishna says, yes. Like this. Come, become the horse. Only by becoming the horse did he find relief. He went, sulking. Then he was allowed to stay in this group. So the friend, the pure friend, climbs on this shoulder. The Lord is saying, our friend, our companion, because of pure friendship, does not hesitate even to climb on my shoulder. And he says, who are you, the great people. You and I are equal. What great person are you. Let there be nine lakh cows, even if they are with you. Let there be wealth, so what. In playing, all the boys are equal. In this way they scold Krishna. You and I are equal. You and we are the same. So Sri Krishna is the same. The same Lord who rules over Brahma, over Shiva. [Chaitanya-charitamrita]

5
00:20:51,640 --> 00:26:11,450
You have heard the katha in the Chaitanya-charitamrita. Once, Brahma came to Dvaraka to see Lord Krishna. Brahma came, and he said to the doorkeeper, I have come to meet the Lord of Dvaraka. Please go and tell him. The doorkeeper went. He submitted to the Lord, a person has come. He is telling his name as Brahma. He wants to meet you. The Lord is asking, which Brahma are you. Brahma, on hearing it, went mad. Brahma says, let him think in the mind, what has happened today to the keeper of the door. Which Brahma. Are there ten or twenty Brahmas. How has he begun to ask like this today. Then, becoming dull, he said. That is all right. He went and said, he said to the Lord, he is the father of Sanat-kumara. Then the Lord said, all right, let him come. Brahma came. He offered obeisance. He could not touch the Lord's feet. He offered obeisance to the seat of the Lord's feet, with all four of his crowns. By turns. They were saying, by then the eight-faced Brahma had come. And he also began to do the same. By then the sixteen-faced, the thirty-two-faced. In this way Brahmas of thousands, of crores of faces, came there. And by then the Rudras came. Indras of many kinds came. They also, in several numbers. All the gods. And all, as many heads as there were, in that same proportion the body was large. Then the conscious hall of the Lord began to grow. And into it Brahma, Shiva, and Indra, Chandra, the gods, and the rest were contained. All with bodies larger than one another. Krishnadasa Kaviraja Goswami writes, in the middle of those great Brahmas and the Rudras, that father of Sanat-kumara was standing in such a way that it seemed a rabbit was standing among great elephants. The four-faced one. Then the Lord asks, what is it, Rudra. Is the conduct of creation going properly. Yes, it is going properly. This is happening. Then he asks Brahma, the great Brahmas. Is some demon not making a disturbance. In creating, is some difficulty not happening. No, by your mercy all is well. He asks Indra, do you rain properly. Do you maintain the people. The Lord is asking like this. And that father of the Sanakas went numb. His mind was going mad. [Chaitanya-charitamrita]

6
00:26:12,650 --> 00:35:13,410
They make the qualities of these very ones. A quality will have to be made. So all these things are being remembered by Srila Shukadeva Goswami. He is the same Lord whom the great saints meditate on in the form of Brahman. And the associates of the Lord serve. As the supreme deity. The Lord. When you people read in a chapter, in the Gita, this is called the supreme deity. The supreme godhood. Who is creating all, moving all, feeding all, giving all to drink. Brahma, Rudra, and the rest, all are praising him. Brahma is taking birth. Why, why has such fortune come to these children. Because of heaps of performed piety. Heaps of heaps. Groups of groups. They have done piety. And this piety means devotion, devotion of love, that devotion. Hare Krishna, Hare Krishna. The greatest evidence is the Bhagavatam. The evidence without a stain. Shukadeva Goswami, finding the occasion, is hinting here that this is the height of practice. If Sri Krishna is found in the form of one's own friend, if a chance to play with him is received, then this alone is the wealth of life. And other worldly gifts and pieties are included in it. It is not said, leaving them aside, that a great devotion has been done. A person who is a devotee in truth also keeps doing many good acts of this kind. As we heard the other day, that Jadabharata was going along washing the lake. He gives food to the hungry. He gives water to the thirsty. He gives cloth. He gives medicine. Giving happiness to other living beings, this is piety. By enjoying enjoyment, a living being becomes impure. But when he gives to another, piety happens. This has been said. Once a person was doing a great deal with us. He said, giving to another is not necessary. Piety can happen. It can happen that a person puts it into some wrong work. Then I said, yes, giving to others is not piety. You enjoy a great deal. This is piety. You eat a great deal. They have gone on a path. That path is in truth the right one. People read in the Bhagavatam, Maharaj Rantideva was hungry for forty-eight days, and he was in the condition of dying. Still he gave food and water also to another. Today his name is unaging and undying. Maharaj Bali gave everything to the Lord, he surrendered it. Dadhichi gave his bone. He gave his own body for the protection of the gods. Here is the tendency of giving a gift. Giving. In truth he does give. He has learned to give. This is called piety. Although the ordinary is untrue. To worship, to do the devotion of the Lord, and to teach others, to take them, this is the greatest piety. Because in the world the greatest cause of the sorrow of living beings is forgetfulness of Krishna. So one who helps in bringing the memory of Krishna is doing a great piety. So we should do piety of every kind. As much strength as there is, in truth. As long as there is life, let the help be done. Whatever the capacity to help is, let that be done. One who has wealth, let him help with wealth. One who has speech, let him do it with speech. Let him do it by preaching devotion, by preaching the Lord. Or in another way also, by giving a material facility also, let him do it. Let him do it. A man should walk only on the stone of piety, on the stone of human effort. He should never stay on the stone of enjoyments. The enjoyers have never been praised in the world. Maharaj Rantideva gave a gift, and there is great praise of him. But Ravana made a city of gold and enjoyed it, so why is he blamed. He enjoys a great deal, then. In this way the words heaps of performed piety are giving an inspiration to practice. Then the question comes, the Lord gave these children such a fitness, such a fortune, so what was the cause in it. Then the one who gives the meaning of the Bhagavatam, Shukadeva Goswami, says, heaps of performed piety. That in birth after birth they did a very great piety. One should not become satisfied by doing piety. One should not think, I have done a great deal, now what shall I do. However much piety is acquired, it is good. From piety, happiness is found. From piety, the Lord is found. And at least devotion. This is written in the Bhagavatam, that by doing any other great work, austerity, sacrifice, charity, and the rest, the mind is not purified in that way, as it is by the syllables of the name of Hari. As a living being is purified by pronouncing the name of the Lord, he is not purified like that by great works. This point, this thing, the associates of the Lord himself have spoken in the Bhagavatam. It is not that they came from somewhere on this earth, gave a false talk, and went. Human beings speak falsehood. The gods, these associates of the Lord, do not speak falsehood. And a story had also come. A sinner was not allowed to be taken to hell. Those people freed him. Then the messengers of Yamaraja ask, why is this happening. Then the associates of the Lord told, this is not a sinner. The sin of his crores of births has been cut. Several things happened. These people say, he did not take the name on purpose. But the Lord knows that someone is taking my name. The one who chants the name may remember the Lord or may not. But the intelligence is without a distinction. A person who pronounces the name, the Lord accepts him at that same time. He is not one-pointed. But the mind of the Lord always stays one-pointed. He accepts the one who chants the name, he is mine. So the meaning of piety became the pronunciation of the name. This alone purifies. The best of all baths. Let the sankirtan of Sri Krishna be supremely victorious. [Siksastaka 1] The name of the Lord. They are not finding it. They are the Lord's associates, perfect from beginningless time. But in this world some things are said to give people the inspiration of practice. To give inspiration. That we will say, they are playing with the Lord by doing this piety, so other people also. One verse is expressing, we did not receive a chance that I might play with the Lord in this way. That we did not do piety. Or all those people sitting in that assembly have begun to regret. Then can we ever play with Krishna in this way. Shukadeva says, you can play. But one will have to become a heap of performed piety.

7
00:35:14,340 --> 00:41:15,440
The dust of whose feet, even by yogis who have held the self, through the hardship of many births, is not obtained. He himself stands as the object of their eye. What can be said of the fortune of the people of Vraja. [Srimad-Bhagavatam 10.12.12] Doing austerity through very many births, the great yogis, people intent on practice, cannot obtain even one dust of his feet. Not obtained. Even by the great yogis, doing austerity through very many births, even by meditating, the one whose one particle of the feet cannot be obtained, that same Lord, by his own need, by his own wish, has become in front of their eyes. He has become the object of the eye. He is situated in front of the eyes, and he is playing. Who can praise their fortune. That is, I am completely unable. What description can I make of the fortune of those children. What can be said of the fortune of the people of Vraja. Brahma, Shiva, and the rest are also unable to describe the fortune of those children. He himself stands as the object of the eye. Becoming the object of their eyes, the Lord himself is near them. To take the father. He himself is situated. What can be said of the fortune of the people of Vraja. So what description should be made of the good fortune of the residents of Braj. Not of these children. Leave aside the talk of the children's fortune. Vrajaukas. Whoever is a resident of Braj. Even the calves, the peacocks, the bees, the monkeys, and the frogs. Who can praise their fortune, before whose eyes the Lord himself is. A cuckoo, or a bee, or a monkey, or any bird, is more fortunate than any person of another place. And Brahma of another place is also smaller than one monkey of this place. This is the feeling. Then these, Brahma does not receive the sight of the Lord. And in Vrindavan, the cuckoo, the parrot, the chataka, all of these keep seeing the Lord. And not by a great effort. The Lord himself comes into the forest. He comes himself. He has come himself from his own abode, from Goloka, from Vaikuntha. So the Lord is that unobtainable, that rare. Su means one dust. One particle. One particle of whose feet is rare even for those people. By whom. By those who have held the self. By the yogis. Who have brought their own mind under control. Who are able to contemplate the Lord. They do only contemplation. And even for many, one dust of whose feet is unobtainable. They will not be able to obtain it. And that same Lord himself, who has become the object of their eye. In front of the eye he is playing, he is eating, he is laughing, he is speaking. Who can describe the good fortune of those residents of Braj. That is, in this universe there is no one who is able to make this description. What can be said of the fortune of the people of Vraja. What description can be made. Who will do it. So fortunate, blessed, are they who are seeing the Lord. The people of Vraja. All should be understood. Animals, birds, and with them the cowherd men, the gopis, all. The people of Vraja. Peace to the people of Vraja. Of those people of Vraja. The appointed fortune. While speaking the katha, a subject like this comes to Shukadeva Goswami, and there he says, I am unable now to say it. The same, I am unable to describe the fortune of the residents of Braj. I cannot. No one can. Hare Krishna. Glory to Srila Prabhupada. Om bhagavate vasudevaya. Om namo bhagavate vasudevaya. Om bhagavate vasudevaya.

8
00:41:19,920 --> 00:48:18,000
The verse. Then a great demon named Agha attacked. He was unable to bear the sight of their happy play. The meaning of atha is a different beginning. Atha. Now a different beginning is being started in the katha. Until now Shukadeva Goswami was describing the happy play of the children with Sri Krishna. And in playing with the Lord those children had so much absorption that they had forgotten even the food. Then these were children. Children eat early in the morning. But in the play with the Lord so much happiness was being found, in the absorption of happiness they had forgotten the food. It is called the happy play. Then a sight exactly opposed to that happy play is about to come. So the word atha is being used. A sight that breaks the happy play. Atha. There was one great demon. The meaning of maha, everyone knows. What it is. Put maha on all, then it is very large. A demon. But a great demon. A great demon. Until now, however many had come into Braj, for them the word demon had been used. But today, for Aghasura, a great demon. Shukadeva Goswami is saying. He was very wicked, and very powerful. His name was Agha. The meaning of agha is sin. Then it is not known why his family gave the name Agha. Then he will have been like that from the beginning. So his name is Agha. One who may never find a good destination. The act that does not let one go to a good destination, that is agha, sin. It is not known, his priest gave the name, or the parents gave it. Whoever gave it, his name is Agha. A great demon. They are describing his being a demon. This is the nature of demons. They do not receive the training, burn at another's happiness, die on seeing another's rise. So they do not take training. They are like this from birth itself. So it is called an easy nature. The point is, those children were playing, and he could not see their playing. And he thought in the mind, let me eat all of these. This bad thought came in his mind. Unable to bear the sight of their happy play. In seeing the play of their happiness, he could not be patient. Kshama means able. He could not bear it. The cause, he was joining it with his own intelligence, this is the boy, this wicked one, who killed my sister, Putana. And just now he killed my brother Baka. So the younger brother of Baki and of Baka. He was the younger brother of Baki and of Baka. The younger brother. Then a brother, whose sister has been killed, whose brother has been killed, will naturally take revenge. But he was so wicked that he did not consider how that Baki had come, and what this Bakasura wanted to do. He did not consider. A demon. So he did not bear the happy play of these children. Such is the nature of these demons. What is the meaning of nature. The meaning of nature is, without effort, whatever tendency we enter, whatever act, that is called nature. As we people are breathing. This is nature. We are breathing naturally. No one is making a great effort. They eat this, and it is digested. Natural. This is called nature. In the Ramcharitmanas there is one line. Kakabhushundi says to Garuda, helping others, with word, mind, and body. The easy nature of a saint, O king of birds. [Tulsidas, Ramcharitmanas] O lord of birds, Garuda. The easy nature of a saint is helping others. Word, mind, body. With the word, with the body, and with the mind, to help another. That is their easy form. They do not have to be taught. On hearing instruction they do not help others. Doing the human effort by themselves is their nature. And exactly the opposite of this. And of a saint, the nature of a wicked person is, harming others. Word, mind, body. The nature of the wicked is easy, O king of birds. The nature of the wicked is, easily giving pain to someone.

9
00:48:20,940 --> 00:53:38,010
The children were playing in Vrindavan. They were absorbed with so much joy in playing with the Lord. The Lord was playing, so the child is right there. He was so wicked that the gods also, night and day, stayed engaged in this contemplation, when will he die. When will his end come. They were greatly worried. Waiting for his end. His end, or his decay, or the fault, that he die. When he dies, they kept waiting for that. He had given that much. The question comes, what pain did the gods have. The gods cannot die. They are drinkers of nectar. They have drunk the nectar. And otherwise the meaning of having drunk nectar is, it did not happen even once that at the time of the churning of the ocean they received nectar. That is not the only meaning. But still those people waited for his end. Why. Because the gods knew that without the worship of the Lord, life is useless. Dying was not for them, in any way. But they were so disturbed, so disturbed, by that Aghasura, that they were not able to worship the Lord. Having drunk nectar. This is one meaning. They knew that the nectar of Krishna's worship, the nectar of Krishna's katha, was not being found. So all wanted that he die. Then he was a special keeper of Kamsa's order. That talk will come ahead. So the gods also wanted his killing, wanted his end. By this it was proved that the world of the gods also was greatly unhappy from him. It was burning. It was in great pain. But the demon Agha, from the mouth of Lord Krishna. Instructed by Kamsa. The younger brother of both. He, the well-known wicked one. The younger brother of Baki and of Baka. Baki is Putana, Bakasura, he was their younger brother. He was the younger brother. And instructed by Kamsa. First, he himself was wicked. He was Aghasura. He himself was sin embodied. They are telling this point. By nature itself, by the nature of birth after birth, he was agha, he was wicked, he was sin. And whose company did he receive. Of the king of the wicked. Of Kamsa. First, his own nature itself was very wicked. And he received the company of Kamsa, the crown of the wicked. And that same Kamsa was the king. He gave the training. Instructed by Kamsa. He obeyed Kamsa's order very well. As a disciplined student obeys the order of the guru, so completely. Bakasura had also come. He also wanted to eat the children. He had already eaten Krishna. So the impression before birth was full of sin. The company of the heated one happened. And a sinful brother and sister also. So the family also was received like that. The family was received, and the company of Kamsa was received. Shelter, the shelter of the kingdom, was received. He received a very heavy salary, because of doing sin. So, instructed by Kamsa. Disciplined. Kamsa had sent him specially. And when he had come, Kamsa knew everything. The timing. And to the followers of Kamsa, those people taking the news. When he had gone. He was a very famous wicked one. So Shukadeva is giving his introduction like this. Instructed by Kamsa. The younger brother of Baki and of Baka. Aghasura. And he. He means that well-known wicked one.

10
00:53:38,010 --> 00:59:11,090
Then he came. Then this question can come, brother, why does he want to eat all the children. It is because of Krishna. Coming into the forest, into Vrindavan, and hiding in one place, he saw Krishna. This one has destroyed my brother of the same womb. This is he. This is the boy of the evening. He has destroyed my brother of the same womb. Sodara means, he has killed the brother of the same womb. And he has killed the sister of the same womb. This one. This is he, who is thinking in his own mind. Then Shukadeva Goswami, listening carefully near him, is saying, he is speaking like this, he has killed my sister and brother of the same womb. Then for those two. That is, to pay the debt of those two. To become free of the debt of both. I will kill this one. With his strength. With his army. Meaning, with his group. I will kill this one. It should be kept in mind that Balarama has not come today. The Lord did not bring Balarama for grazing the calves. That is good. Whatever his group is, I will kill this one with all of them. So much enmity toward the Lord. Then, he has destroyed my brother of the same womb. So I will kill this one with his strength. If I kill one, the revenge will not be paid by that. As he has killed my brother, has killed my sister, I will pay interest many times over. By killing all the companions. And there were thousands and thousands of children. He has made a plan to kill all. Then he says, when these die, when these children die, then their mothers, fathers, relatives, will die in the same way. As when the root of a tree is pulled out, the branch, the leaf, the flower, all die. This is the life. This is the life of the children. And these children, they are the life of their own mothers and fathers. When they hear that all these children have died, then the great cowherd men or the gopis, by themselves. When all these children are made the offering of sesame and water for our friends. The sesame offering. The meaning of tilodaka is the handful of sesame. Tilodaka, which is given to the dead. The offering of the rice ball is made. And all grass. To these alone, in place of drops of water, let me give milk. When the sesame and water have been offered, meaning when they have been killed, then the people of Vraja are as if destroyed. Then however many other residents of Braj there are, they are as if destroyed. They are understood as finished. They will not live either, then they will live crying ha ha. In their living, what profit. The children will die, then those people will become like a body without life. The offspring itself is the life-breath. The life also, these are yours. In this world, however many beings there are, those people have the offspring itself as the life-breath. The offspring itself is their life-breath, their life. One's own child, a great deal. Then she will become like a dead person. This is the means of killing all. In this way he decided. Keep hearing, what kind of decision the demons make. If someone had made a means of killing the great elders, had killed them, then it would be another matter. He has given playing children to be eaten. How they were one plow. His sister was like this. She would kill children by putting poison on the breast. These wicked people never see the fault of their own kinsmen. What our brother was like, and what our sister was like. They never consider.

