00:59:11,610 --> 01:05:41,790
It is written in the Ramayana also. When the Lord had Lakshmana cut Surpanakha's ear and her nose, she went weeping to Ravana. First she had gone to some other people. When those people died, then she went to Ravana. Going to Ravana, she began to weep. And weeping, she says, while you live, ten-necked one, how has this fate of mine happened. O ten-headed one, in your lifetime, this misery of your sister. Such a misery has been done. You are there. If someone fights, then someone will cut, then he will cut one head. Nine will remain. This is the point. Having ten heads, what have you done. You have twenty eyes, and ten heads. But in your lifetime this is our misery. Just consider. Do this. I once saw a play of the Ramayana. In it Ravana's court was seated. And Surpanakha was going, screaming, weeping. And blood was flowing from the nose. From the ear. All of that was put into a dramatic form. Whatever it was. Then the play went very well. Taking which, she was provoking Ravana, that two boys have come, and without a crime, without an offense, they have cut our nose and ear. The consideration did not begin, who he is, how they went, where they cut. Then she says, the one of Nashik of Panchavati. Nashik received the name later. Her nose was cut, and after that the name Nashik. But she was saying, here in the Dandaka forest, in Panchavati, our nose and ear were cut. Then at that time. Then a good point. A jester was made in Ravana's court. The jester said, government, forgive me, then let me ask you one thing. He said it to Ravana. Ravana said, come, all right, all right. Speak. He said, what was the cause of Surpanakha's going to Panchavati. Let this be asked a little. There will have been some feeling. Please ask her why she went on the journey to Panchavati. Ravana heard, and became a little grave. But after that he did not give attention. He did not ask. Leave it, this is not the time for what curiosity. There is an answer. Then he called the physician. He said, treat her nose and ear. Do this. And Ravana went to sleep. At night sleep was not coming to him. Who is that person who cut the nose and the ear. This was done, that was done. Then at that same time, without asking anyone, he went to his uncle. To Maricha. And he sent him. Giving the order, you test. Who he is. Become a deer of illusion. If he follows you, to catch you, then I will understand that he is a human being. Then I will snatch his wife and bring her. And I will bring her. Then Maricha said, it is like this, nephew. Then Ravana says, I have not come as your nephew. I am a king. Say, Your Majesty. Then Maricha says, Your Majesty. I know those boys. He is not the knower of the sacrifice. And Rama is the Supreme Brahman. He is the Lord. We have the experience. They, to us. Mother, then they will kill us. They will finish us from life. Do not do this. You return home. You are a king, or whatever you are. But you are our nephew. I am your uncle. I am giving you this teaching. Beautiful. I am instructing you. You should stay alive. He said, are you going or not. Then he saw his own death on both sides. Then he took shelter of the leader of the Raghus. Then he saw, on this side also he will kill. On going there, Rama will kill. Then he thought, dying by Rama's hand is right. Let me go. Then Rama did not consider anything. All right. And he did not accept. So in this way, the intention of my saying is that wicked people do not consider at all the wickedness of the people of their own family. Now this one is seeing that this boy has killed my brother, has killed my sister. But what did the sister and the brother do. Did the boy go and kill in Mathura. Those people used to come here to make a disturbance. They would come into Braj, make a disturbance, and die. But he is thinking in this way. When the sesame offering is made for the brother and sister of my friend. The sesame and water. What is the report. It is now. Then those who hold life take their own child, their own people, as their own life.

