01:05:41,790 --> 01:12:28,590
Having decided thus, a python of a vast body. A yojana in measure. Thick as a great mountain. Having taken an astonishing form. A mouth of a cave, wide open. Then the wicked one lay on the path, with the wish to swallow. So the children, playing, were going ahead on the path they were advancing on. The calves were walking ahead, grazing, spread out. And the children were going behind, playing. They were advancing somewhat. As the calves were advancing, so they were also going while playing. Wherever they were going, right there on the road, on the path, he lay down, having become a very large python. He lay down, having become a snake. Having decided thus. A python, a vast body. He was one yojana in measure. He was four kos. If you look even at the length alone, he was four kos. He was eight miles long. But here the meaning of measure is, if that serpent were to bend, then he was eight miles. Not the circumference alone. The meaning of measure is his reach, his width, his thickness, whatever it is. He was that vast. One yojana is four kos, eight miles. And thick as a great mountain. And how thick he was. Thick. He was as thick as one great mountain. He was high. Wide, thick, very high. A great mountain. Having become like a very large mountain, having taken the body of a python. And he lay on the path. He lay specially on the path. Having taken an astonishing form. A mouth of a cave, wide open. He took the astonishing body of a python, and he lay on the road. With the wish to swallow. To swallow the children, the calves, Krishna, all of them. He lay down in order to eat them in his own mouth. And his mouth is one. According to that it will be very deep, it will be large. He lay down in the likeness of the cave of a vast mountain. Then he is establishing his being astonishing. The lower lip on the ground, the upper lip a cloud. The lower lip was said. On the ground. The lower lip. His lower lip is the lower one. On the ground. Clouds would strike. He made the upper lip that high. In this way, tearing the mouth open, he lay down. The interior of the lips, and the teeth like mountain peaks. And the interior, what the edge of his mouth was like. Like the valley of a mountain. Like a gorge. And what the teeth were like. His teeth, large like a mountain. That dreadful. And the interior of darkness. His mouth was such that a thick darkness was filled in it. The inside of his mouth was filled with thick darkness. A spread-out forked tongue. How the forked tongue had come out. He had made it just like a road, pressed to the ground. Then the children fell into confusion. They did not recognize whether this is a road or a living being, of a snake. One spread-out tongue like a road. Like a path of great expanse, a wide path, like a road, his tongue was. Then a tongue is thin. His tongue was very wide. Of his body. As a fire catches in a forest, and from there the hope comes, and a bad smell comes. Many living beings burn in a forest fire. Then the bad smell of their bodies comes. So in this way he had eaten many living beings, so his breath was coming out like that. The breath was feeling like the wind of a forest fire. And the eye like a forest fire. His eye was red. So it seemed that on the mountain a forest fire was burning. A fire was burning. In this way a very hot wind was coming from his belly. The breath he is letting out. By which this confusion happened to the children. People call Krishna agha today. Gala and gara are one word. In Sanskrit a difference is not accepted between ra and la. Say gara, or say gala. Then he thought, when people call this one agha, he is agha, then we have to keep agha in our own throat. Then what is to be kept in the throat, is to be eaten. Then my these are meaningful. The craft. He has become a python. They make this meaning. It is possible this same thing will have come in his mind. So he has lain down, having become a python.

