01:25:47,730 --> 01:31:56,960
And what is the Lord thinking inside. The Lord was thinking, now let me stop them, let me save them, let me save them. By then all these are finished. This is the condition. Shukadeva Goswami is describing in this way. Having seen. Up to patience. The clapping should not be done. They do the clapping. They clap. Come, come, come. We will see a new beauty. We will see a new beauty. Let us enter it. In this way, speaking what was untrue to one another, having heard, having considered, this which seems false is not false. Knowing it to be a demon, he who stays in the heart of every being, the Lord fixed his mind to stop his own. When the children were talking with one another in this way. What were they talking. Untrue. In their talk there was no fact. They were understanding that this is a mountain. It is some beauty of Vrindavan. It is a natural beauty. But the Lord was understanding that they are speaking what is untrue. All. In truth that was a serpent. They were not seeing the serpent in this way. It is looking like a mountain, it is looking. But yes, a python. They were not seeing it in this form. They were thinking, it is a mountain, and it is looking like a python. This is called spoken as untrue. Those who did not know Aghasura. Those children, about Aghasura, making him a mountain and a cave and the rest, are speaking in this way. The Lord considered, how is this seeming to them. This is not false. Amrisha means true. In truth it is a python. And a python swallows how many people. But it is also a demon. The Lord understood, this is a demon. How did he understand. Because he stays in the heart of every being. The Lord lives in the heart of all living beings. Situated in the heart of all beings. Situated in the heart of every being. The Lord is in the heart of all living beings, in the form of the Supersoul. So he had understood long before that this is a demon. And the demon, having become a python, wants to swallow all. And these children, false, false, are coming. To these people, a false thing. It is a python, and he is understanding the python as a mountain. And a great deal, their own bravery, their own learning, the children are going along proclaiming. It is looking like teeth. It is looking like a tongue. And the teeth are there. What is it looking like. The tongue, and the jaw, and a forest fire is burning. This is burning. But one thing is there, the children trust Krishna a great deal. If it swallows, Bakari is with us. This will be destroyed now. A daring of this kind. They were keeping faith in the Lord. Not by understanding him as the Lord. They were thinking this. Bakasura has died just now. At the very end. So they say Bakari. The enemy of Baka. They would also call Krishna Bakari, Bakari. That this is the enemy of Baka. A new event had happened. So this one will die now. Then the Lord understood that this is a demon. The Lord fixed his mind to stop his own. They were coming. By then they had entered the belly of the animal. He was thinking, let me stop them, let me stop them. By then all had entered. Into the belly of the demon. All had gone into the belly of Aghasura. But not swallowed. The children, with the calves. But he did not swallow them. Swallowed means, he did not gulp them. But the meaning of swallowing is this, it is a snake, when it swallows someone, at the end it contracts the mouth. It closes it. And it twists its own body like that. In Sanskrit they say motana. That is the twisting of the limbs. In this way it bends its own limb. It gathers it. So that even the bone of that living being breaks in it. A snake has no bone. A snake has only the scale. But in this way a python, or some snake, wraps its own body, breaks, so that inch by inch, little by little, it breaks the bone, it gives the obstruction, by its own body. It does not chew with the teeth. With the teeth, someone catches. So the twisting of the limbs he had not done yet. He has thought, if I close my own mouth, Krishna will flee. They are seeing that this is a python. He was understanding, if he will understand us as a mountain itself, then all the other children have gone in. So the mouth, as he had opened it, he kept it open. And he also did not do the twisting of the body. Meaning, he also did not bend the limb. Otherwise Krishna could have sprung. He could have fled. They would have fled. And what its aim was, the real one, that jam, as they say, keeps going. It is not completed. So as he had slept, so he stayed asleep. He did not loosen. So the children went straight in, just like the cave of a mountain. He did not drop these teeth on them. Like a mill, or like a peak, whatever it was. And he did not break and twist them. The children. This, supreme. They only entered. They only entered. Not swallowed. They were not gulped. Swallowed means to gulp. But Shukadeva Goswami is saying for this reason that they were not gulped. That the snake in truth did nothing. These people entered. Then the entrance. This sitting stops here.
